blers: a randomized controlled trial</article-title><source>J Gambl Stud</source><year>2007</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>215</fpage><lpage>230</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17245662</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s10899-006-9052-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lorenz</surname><given-names>VC</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Galaski T</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Family dynamics of pathological gamblers</article-title><source>The handbook of pathological gambling</source><year>1987</year><publisher-name>Springfield IL: Charles C. Thomas</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lorenz</surname><given-names>VC</given-names></name><name><surname>Yaffee</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pathological gambling: psychosomatic, emotional and marital difficulties as reported by the spouse</article-title><source>Journal of Gambling Behavior</source><year>1988</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>13</fpage><lpage>26</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF01043525</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>EE</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamer</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Nora</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Tan</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Eisenstein</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Engelhart</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Lie/Bet Questionnaire for screening pathological gamblers</article-title><source>Psychol Rep</source><year>1997</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>83</fpage><lpage>88</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9122356</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2466/PR0.80.1.83-88</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>G&#x000f6;testam</surname><given-names>KG</given-names></name><name><surname>Johansson</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Wenzel</surname><given-names>HG</given-names></name><name><surname>Simonsen</surname><given-names>IE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Validation of the lie/bet screen for pathological gambling on two normal population data sets</article-title><source>Psychol Rep</source><year>2004</year><volume>95</volume><fpage>1009</fpage><lpage>1013</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15666948</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2466/PR0.95.7.1009-1013</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>Statistics Norway. Norwegian Standard Classification of Education</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.ssb.no/emner/04/90/nos_c617/"/></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schou</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name><name><surname>Krokstad</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Westin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hva betyr selvopplevd helse for d&#x000f8;dligheten?</article-title><source>Tidsskr Nor L&#x000e6;geforen</source><year>2006</year><volume>126</volume><fpage>2644</fpage><lpage>2647</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Orford</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Templeton</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Velleman</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Copello</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Family members of relatives with alcohol, drug and gambling problems: a set of standardized questionnaires for assessing stress, coping and strain</article-title><source>Addiction</source><year>2005</year><volume>100</volume><fpage>1611</fpage><lpage>1624</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16277623</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1360-0443.2005.01178.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rychtarik</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name><name><surname>McGillicuddy</surname><given-names>NB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Preliminary Evaluation of a Coping Skills Training Program for Those with a Pathological-Gambling Partner</article-title><source>J Gambl Stud</source><year>2006</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>165</fpage><lpage>178</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s10899-006-9008-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Makarchuk</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hodgins</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Peden</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Development of a brief intervention for concerned significant others of problem gamblers</article-title><source>Addictive Disorders and Their Treatment</source><year>2002</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>126</fpage><lpage>134</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00132576-200211000-00003</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>